From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_L2PF=1 reads a decode window's next weights
 into L2 on a side stream (upstream port)

Ported onto f350cd3 + patches 0001-0112 from upstream ashhart/TensorFold:
  8cc6ac420 glm cuda: TF_GLM_L2PF reads a decode window's next weights into L2 on a side stream while gathers and chains run (Bizuayeu)
  a0ddae24d glm cuda: TF_GLM_L2PF's two launches carry nvcc 13.0 contract records (Bizuayeu)

Opt-in, off by default. Upstream's later default-on commits (96e9ebf29, e26a99ad1) are not taken: the prefetch is not
yet qualified on this patched engine. Each decode window of a rank alone has three sites: n before gather_b reads the
next layer's mixer input (KDA's qkv scales, codes and bf16 rest, or DSA's proj and q_b), f before gather_a reads this
layer's ffn head (the router, or a dense layer's gate and up), and o between KDA's projections and its chain reads its
o. EXL3 routed experts are not prefetched. Rows are the weights' own allocations after they tile, within
TF_GLM_L2PF_MB (12) a site; the kernels are DeepSeek V4.1's l2pf (TF_GLM_L2PF_CTAS, 2) and l2pace
(TF_GLM_L2PF_PACE_GBPS, 150; 0 unpaced). The side stream only reads, and joins the main stream once at the window's end.

Port notes: Settings, Fingerprint and the Forward fields keep patches 0041/0064/0110's members (numerics, kv_shard) and
add l2pf beside them; the Fingerprint layout goes 15 -> 16 (the recipe's own numbering, not upstream's 18). The shared
window's KDA mixer forks site o before the batched chains of patches 0075/0088. Upstream-only fields that came with the
hunk context (roce_multi, kv_host, solo, share_pages) are not taken. The contract records join landed_cuda after
penalty_sampling. Local addition: L2pf.deinit drains the side stream before destroying it.

On the four-Spark stack (tp4-local): the dense ffn's sources also take block FP8's gate/up (0107's fp8g), as MXFP8's.

Co-authored-by: Bizuayeu <30091157+Bizuayeu@users.noreply.github.com>
